We implement our own solvers from the problem definitions in problems.py:

  * solve_coloring: exhaustive search over 3^n colourings.
  * solve_sat: complete DPLL search (unit propagation), cross-checked on
    small formulas against a 2^m brute force.

Then we compare the answers on many small source instances and their
reductions, and also validate the produced target instances.
